  "details": "At least for friends, otherwise favoriting your friends avatars may get overcomplicated as they would need to make a avatar world or having you to come to you and clone you.\nI know this always was the intended way and can help prevent *some* interactions but i bet most clients and websites have their own database anyway that they crawl avatar ids for.\nRemoving this completely without any reasonable response other than \"the api will and might break\" doesnt seem fair imo. Ofc if you had the wrong friends they could still clone your public avatars then, but whats the point? If people want an avatar they would probably just rip it then or use such brutrforced databases to get the avatars details. This api change only serves the purpose anyway if you ever be in private worlds. Please bring this Feature back. \nall removing it got certain sites to implement payed downloading of avatar files. gg\n\nThanks",
